<h2>Hidalgo County and TWIA</h2>
<p>The Texas Windstorm Insurance Association (TWIA) provides wind and hail coverage only in designated coastal counties, including neighboring Cameron and Willacy counties. <strong>Hidalgo County is not in the TWIA area.</strong> McAllen properties typically get wind coverage from their regular insurer, or from the Texas FAIR Plan where applicable, and TDI windstorm (WPI-8) certification does not apply here. Details are on the <a href="https://www.twia.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TWIA website</a>.</p>

<h2>Typical Documentation for a Hurricane Claim</h2>
<ul>
<li>Photos and video of every elevation and room, with water lines clearly shown if flooding occurred.</li>
<li>Evidence showing where water entered: roof openings and broken windows versus water rising from the ground.</li>
<li>NOAA and NWS storm records for the event.</li>
<li>Mitigation invoices, moisture readings, and drying logs.</li>
<li>Receipts for hotel stays, meals, and other additional living expenses.</li>
<li>Contents inventory and an itemized building estimate.</li>
<li>Copies of every policy: homeowners or commercial, flood, and any separate wind coverage.</li>
</ul>
<p>Our <a href="/claim-documentation-checklist/">claim documentation checklist</a> can help.</p>

<h2>Common Claim Issues and Insurer Arguments</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Wind vs. flood.</strong> The property insurer attributes damage to excluded flood; the flood insurer attributes it to wind. Clear evidence of each cause is essential. See <a href="/water-damage-vs-flood-damage-mcallen/">water damage vs. flood damage</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Anti-concurrent causation language.</strong> Some policies exclude damage caused by flood even when wind contributed. Policy wording controls.</li>
<li><strong>Deductible disputes.</strong> Whether a named storm deductible or the standard wind/hail deductible applies.</li>
<li><strong>Pre-existing damage.</strong> The insurer says roof leaks existed before the storm.</li>
<li><strong>Delays.</strong> Catastrophe claim volume can slow inspections and payments. See <a href="/services/delayed-insurance-claims/">delayed insurance claims</a>.</li>
</ul>

